  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Partenaire relais - RISoL</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The &quot;Social Innovation Network for Local Resilience&quot; (RISoL) project aims to strengthen the capacities of civil society organizations in the governorates of Kebili, Tozeur, and Gafsa, with a particular focus on supporting young people and women. The first step isto create a support and social innovation network, promoting networking between CSOs and local stakeholders, while facilitating theexchange of expertise and strategic collaboration. Then, the project will set up an innovative incubation offer, adapted to the specific needs of the beneficiaries, adopting a proximity approach for personalized support. This system will allow CSOs to benefit from training, mentoring and resources to better support local initiatives and strengthen community resilience. The ultimate goal is tocreate sustainable dynamics that empower vulnerable populations and support long-term local development. The project also includes a structural component that aims to provide the Al Bacikat team with the necessary skills in Project Management Professional (According to the ISO 21500 standard, AGIL Scrum), while ensuring the effective implementation of the procedures manual developed within the framework of the structural fund of the ROSE project.</narrative>
  </description>
  <participating-org role="4" type="90">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Association AL Bacikat Pour le</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The association was created in September 2012 in a rural community in the governorate of K&#xe9;bili and affects the regions of Tozeur and Gabes. Their objective is to work on development projects. The association focuses their work on young people and women.The objectives of this association are sustainable development, gender equality, raising women&apos;s awareness of their economic rights, the empowerment of women, the reduction of inequalities and poverty and respect for the environment.</narrative>
  </participating-org>
